{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b4a2151f-db8d-46b9-946b-a02face2a6e5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-853e6aa56b2e1c72","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-59hfl4mw/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E001.md","content":"# Validate mid-run availability of benchmark status in the EvalHub job detail API\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the strategy's flagged open question: does the EvalHub Server detail endpoint (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) populate `status.benchmarks[]` entries — per-benchmark status with `started_at`/`completed_at` — while an evaluation job is still running, or only after the job completes? The answer determines which progress-display implementation is built: a detail-polling layer with benchmark-level progress (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") and elapsed time derived from per-benchmark `started_at`, or an elapsed-time-only display computed from `resource.created_at` on the list endpoint. The strategy's assumption that the array is populated mid-run is explicitly marked \"needs validation\", and the Staff Engineer Input's field-availability table documents only that the field exists in the response schema, not when it is populated during execution.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Determine, from the EvalHub Server source code (the job status write paths) and, where feasible, observed API responses, when `status.benchmarks[]` entries are created and updated over a job's lifecycle.\n- Document which fields are present per benchmark entry mid-run (status values, `started_at`, `completed_at`) and whether entries appear at benchmark start, update incrementally, or appear only at completion.\n- Capture sample detail-endpoint responses for a job in a non-terminal (running) state where a live environment is available.\n- Record the outcome so the branch selection for the progress-display work is unambiguous: mid-run population (detail polling with benchmark progress) or completion-only population (elapsed-time-only display), including any partial-population behavior discovered.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A findings report states whether `status.benchmarks[]` is populated while a job is in a running state or only upon completion, with cited evidence (EvalHub Server source references and/or captured detail-endpoint responses from a running job).\n- Where mid-run population occurs, the report documents which per-benchmark fields are present mid-run and when entries appear or update relative to benchmark start/completion.\n- The report identifies any partial-population behavior (e.g., entries appearing at benchmark start but status updating only at completion) and states which progress-display presentation that behavior supports.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (P1, benchmark-level progress display): this investigation determines whether HLR-4 is deliverable against the existing API.\n- HLR-5 (P1, elapsed time display): determines the timestamp source (per-benchmark `started_at` vs `resource.created_at`) for the elapsed-time computation.\n- HLR-1 (P0, auto-refresh/detail polling portion): determines whether the detail-polling layer has mid-run data to fetch.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":68828,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9970d42ea05d3b5f","agent_id":"a9be68a0f929ee067","session_id":"f9ae5287-b92a-4025-94c1-a1778be86910","uuid":"0ce5034c-c8b6-4091-8b7a-fff2cb1fa85b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:27:22.018Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
