{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b4a2151f-db8d-46b9-946b-a02face2a6e5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-964bd69a56cbc457","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-59hfl4mw/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E002.md","content":"# Catalogue EvalHub failure message codes for pre-start vs runtime failures\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the strategy's flagged open question: what values does `status.message.message_code` take in the EvalHub job list/detail responses, and do those values reliably distinguish pre-start failures (admission errors, scheduling failures, resource constraints) from runtime failures? The answer determines whether the UI can render \"Failed (not started)\" as a visually distinct state from runtime \"Failed\", or must fall back to a single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail — a fallback the strategy already defines in its risk table.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Enumerate the values `status.message.message_code` can take, from the EvalHub Server source code (the error paths that construct status messages) and the published API reference.\n- Classify each value as indicating a pre-start failure (admission error, scheduling failure, resource quota/constraint), a runtime failure, or unclassifiable from the code alone.\n- Where a live environment is available, capture observed `message_code` values from jobs that failed before start and jobs that failed during execution.\n- Produce a recommendation stating whether the pre-start vs runtime distinction is reliably implementable in the UI from `message_code` alone, enabling the gated failure-distinction work to proceed or be removed in favor of the defined fallback.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A catalogue lists the `status.message.message_code` values attainable in list and detail endpoint responses, each with its meaning and a source citation (EvalHub Server source and/or API reference).\n- Every catalogued value is classified as pre-start failure, runtime failure, or unclassifiable.\n- A recommendation states whether the pre-start vs runtime failure distinction is implementable from `message_code` alone, and — if not — explicitly confirms the fallback of a single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P2, pre-start vs runtime failure distinction): this investigation determines whether HLR-7 is implementable as specified or falls back to the single-state rendering.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":68828,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9970d42ea05d3b5f","agent_id":"a9be68a0f929ee067","session_id":"f9ae5287-b92a-4025-94c1-a1778be86910","uuid":"8237b73b-2c4d-48b6-b219-c1dfef5fc17c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:27:28.311Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
