{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-31af6d72-a9bc-4f5e-96cd-551671accfa5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b47825a7ec044728","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-59hfl4mw/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E003.md","content":"# Progress indicator and job state UX specification for the EvalHub Evaluations page\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic produces the \"progress indicator UX specification\" design document that the strategy lists as to-be-created, authored by UX/Design. It defines the visual and interaction patterns the EvalHub Evaluations landing page implementations build against: state icon/color/label treatments for queued/pending, running, failed, and completed jobs, the progress indicator pattern (elapsed time primary, benchmark completion count supplementary), the \"Failed (not started)\" variant treatment, and the non-blocking warning pattern for temporarily unavailable status updates — all aligned to PatternFly.\n\n## Scope\n\n- State visual specifications: distinct PatternFly Label/Icon/color treatments for queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states derived from the list endpoint's `status.state`, including a \"Failed (not started)\" variant distinct from runtime \"Failed\".\n- Progress indicator pattern for running jobs: elapsed time as the primary indicator (mitigating the single-benchmark-job risk, where benchmark completion shows only 0% or 100%), with benchmark completion count (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") as supplementary when available. The pattern must cover both the benchmark-progress presentation and the elapsed-time-only presentation.\n- Non-blocking inline warning pattern for transient polling errors: PatternFly Alert variant \"warning\", rendered while stale (last successful) data continues to display.\n- PatternFly alignment review across the above, using the dashboard design system conventions.\n- The specification is written to hold under either outcome of the benchmark data-availability validation (elapsed-time-primary is the presentation in both cases), so it does not wait on that investigation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The specification defines icon, color, and label treatments for queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states, each visually distinct per the PatternFly status pattern.\n- The specification defines the \"Failed (not started)\" treatment as distinguishable from the runtime \"Failed\" treatment.\n- The specification defines the progress indicator pattern with elapsed time as the primary indicator and benchmark completion count as supplementary.\n- The specification defines the non-blocking inline warning pattern for temporarily unavailable status updates using PatternFly Alert variant \"warning\".\n- The specification is completed and accepted by the ODH Dashboard implementing team as the build-against reference for the evaluations page UI work.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- No HLR is delivered solely by this epic; it is the design prerequisite for HLR-2 (P0, state visual distinction), HLR-4 and HLR-5 (P1, benchmark progress and elapsed time display), and HLR-7 (P2, failure distinction). Functional delivery of those HLRs occurs in the implementation epics that consume this specification.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":70243,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9970d42ea05d3b5f","agent_id":"a9be68a0f929ee067","session_id":"f9ae5287-b92a-4025-94c1-a1778be86910","uuid":"908ae236-86cd-443d-a5aa-89c6171b7d27","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:27:39.703Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
