{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-31af6d72-a9bc-4f5e-96cd-551671accfa5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-835656a31b49b39d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-59hfl4mw/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E004.md","content":"# State visual differentiation for the EvalHub evaluations job list\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers visually distinct state treatments on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page job table, derived from the list endpoint's `status.state` and `status.message` fields: queued/pending, running, failed, and completed, each with a distinct PatternFly status icon, color, and label per the UX specification. It also delivers the fallback failure rendering — a single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail — which stands on its own if the finer pre-start/runtime failure distinction proves unimplementable.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Render state labels, icons, and color treatments for queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states from the list endpoint's `status.state` field, per the UX specification's state treatments.\n- Display error context from `status.message` on failed job rows.\n- Render the baseline single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail where failure classification is not available (the defined fallback).\n- Preserve the existing list-endpoint polling (30s via `useFetchState`) and table rendering behavior unchanged — the state differentiation is additive (backwards-compatibility NFR).\n- No detail-endpoint polling is introduced in this epic; this scope uses only list-endpoint fields, whose availability is confirmed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Job rows display a distinct label, icon, and color for each of queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states derived from `status.state`, visually distinguishable from each other per the UX specification.\n- A job transitioning from running to complete is reflected in the job list within the existing list-endpoint polling interval (30 seconds) without manual browser refresh, measured by the row's state label updating automatically.\n- Failed job rows display error context from `status.message`.\n- Where failure classification is unavailable, the row renders the single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail.\n- The existing list-endpoint polling and table rendering continue to function unchanged.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0, auto-refresh showing state transitions without manual refresh): delivers the top-level state-transition visibility driven by the existing list-endpoint polling. (The detail-polling portion of HLR-1 is delivered by the branch-conditional progress work.)\n- HLR-2 (P0, visual distinction between queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states): primary delivery.\n- HLR-7 (P2, pre-start vs runtime failure distinction): delivers the fallback baseline rendering only; the distinction itself is delivered by the gated failure-distinction work.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":70243,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9970d42ea05d3b5f","agent_id":"a9be68a0f929ee067","session_id":"f9ae5287-b92a-4025-94c1-a1778be86910","uuid":"f2e765ee-9754-4753-aaec-3d5e5646161b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:27:47.253Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
