{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-31af6d72-a9bc-4f5e-96cd-551671accfa5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a29c9d122c8c0407","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-59hfl4mw/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E005.md","content":"# Pre-start vs runtime failure distinction in the evaluations job list\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the finer failure-state distinction on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page: rendering \"Failed (not started)\" — with a label, icon, and color distinct from runtime \"Failed\" — for jobs whose `status.message.message_code` indicates a pre-start failure (admission error, scheduling failure, resource constraint), per the validated message-code catalogue and the UX specification's failure-variant treatment. If the catalogue finds the values do not reliably distinguish failure types, this epic is removed and the fallback (single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text) delivered by the state differentiation work stands.\n\n## Description of Dependencies\n\nThis epic is gated on the validated `message_code` semantics catalogue and builds on the state rendering surface delivered by the state differentiation work and its UX specification; those must resolve first.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Apply the validated `status.message.message_code` classification to failed job rows: render \"Failed (not started)\" where the code indicates a pre-start failure (admission error, scheduling failure, resource constraint), and runtime \"Failed\" otherwise.\n- Render the distinct label, icon, and color for the \"Failed (not started)\" variant per the UX specification's failure treatments.\n- Where `message_code` is ambiguous or absent, fall back to the single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail.\n- No new API fields, enum values, or server-side changes — the distinction works within the existing list-endpoint data (strategy constraint).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a job that failed before execution started, with `status.message.message_code` classified as a pre-start failure per the validated catalogue, the job row displays a \"Failed (not started)\" treatment with label, icon, and color distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state.\n- Given a job that ran and then failed, the job row displays the runtime \"Failed\" treatment.\n- Where `message_code` is ambiguous or absent, the job row falls back to the single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P2, pre-start vs runtime failure distinction using `status.message.message_code` where available): primary delivery.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":70243,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9970d42ea05d3b5f","agent_id":"a9be68a0f929ee067","session_id":"f9ae5287-b92a-4025-94c1-a1778be86910","uuid":"ed7ca75f-0235-40a1-85d4-921ac03fc94e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:27:54.316Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
