{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-2b769fc6-ffa9-4b21-a257-8ee864c5c4e6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-82df0853e8f80409","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-59hfl4mw/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-BRANCH-A-E006.md","content":"# Detail-polling layer with benchmark progress and elapsed time for in-progress evaluation jobs\n\n## Description\n\nBranch A of the progress-display work, selected if the benchmark data-availability investigation confirms that `status.benchmarks[]` is populated in the EvalHub detail endpoint (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) while a job is running. This epic delivers the new detail-polling layer for the Evaluations landing page: a hook that identifies non-terminal jobs on the currently displayed table page and fetches their detail endpoints on a 10-second cycle with a maximum of 5 concurrent requests in round-robin, adopting the React Query retry-with-backoff pattern established by the autorag package. It renders benchmark-level progress (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\"), elapsed time from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps, and a non-blocking inline warning during transient errors. Polling pauses when the browser tab is backgrounded.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Detail-polling hook targeting only non-terminal jobs on the currently displayed table page (client-side pagination: default 20 rows, options 5/10/20); changing the table page immediately retargets which jobs are polled.\n- Concurrency control: maximum 5 concurrent detail requests per user session, dispatched in round-robin (as one request completes, the next pending job is fetched); a 10-second timer starts after all detail fetches for the current page complete, before the next cycle.\n- Retry-on-error per the autorag `usePipelineRunQuery` pattern: `placeholderData` preserving the last successful response, exponential backoff with jitter up to the configured maximum retries, 4xx errors treated as non-retryable, 5xx/network errors retried; a single failed request does not stop the round-robin (partial progress data is acceptable).\n- Non-blocking inline warning (PatternFly Alert variant \"warning\") while status updates are temporarily unavailable, with the last successfully fetched data still displayed.\n- Benchmark-level progress display: \"Benchmarks: X/N complete\" where X is the count of `status.benchmarks[]` entries with status \"completed\", presented as supplementary to the elapsed-time primary indicator per the UX specification.\n- Elapsed time display: client-side difference between current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` across benchmarks (falling back to `resource.created_at` if no benchmark has started).\n- Page Visibility API integration: polling pauses when the tab is backgrounded and resumes with an immediate single polling cycle on focus; polling stops for terminal-state jobs.\n- Until the first detail fetch returns for a job, the row shows only the top-level state from the list endpoint (graceful degradation if the detail endpoint is unavailable).\n- Verification (passive component validation): confirm the odh-dashboard BFF proxy passes through all detail response fields from the eval-hub plugin backend — including `status.benchmarks[]` — without filtering; no BFF code change is expected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a running job with 3 of 5 benchmarks completed and a completed detail-polling cycle for that job, the row displays benchmark-level progress (\"Benchmarks: 3/5 complete\"), measured by the count matching the number of `status.benchmarks[]` entries with status \"completed\" in the detail response.\n- Given a job running for 4 minutes with a completed detail fetch, elapsed time is displayed (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\"), measured by the difference between current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` in the detail response.\n- At most 5 detail requests are in flight concurrently per user session, targeted only at non-terminal jobs on the currently displayed table page; changing the table page immediately updates which jobs are polled.\n- Given a 5xx or network error on a detail fetch, the last successfully fetched progress remains displayed, a non-blocking inline warning (PatternFly Alert variant \"warning\") is visible, the round-robin continues with the next in-progress job, and the failed request retries with exponential backoff up to the configured maximum; 4xx errors are not retried.\n- While the browser tab is backgrounded, no requests are made to the detail endpoint (verified via browser dev tools Network tab); on tab focus, a single polling cycle runs immediately.\n- Polling stops for jobs that reach a terminal state.\n- The React Query retry pattern is validated in the eval-hub Module Federation context by simulating 5xx errors from the BFF on individual detail endpoints (risk-mitigation validation; failure means fix-and-retry within this epic).\n- The BFF proxy is verified to pass through all detail response fields, including `status.benchmarks[]`, without filtering.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0, auto-refresh mechanism — detail endpoint polling portion): primary delivery of the detail-polling layer.\n- HLR-3 (P0, non-blocking error handling during detail polling): retry with exponential backoff, stale data preserved, inline warning.\n- HLR-4 (P1, benchmark-level progress display with max-5 round-robin fetch): primary delivery.\n- HLR-5 (P1, elapsed time display from per-benchmark `started_at`): primary delivery.\n- HLR-6 (P1, polling pauses on backgrounded tab and resumes on focus): primary delivery.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":72315,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9970d42ea05d3b5f","agent_id":"a9be68a0f929ee067","session_id":"f9ae5287-b92a-4025-94c1-a1778be86910","uu