{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-2b769fc6-ffa9-4b21-a257-8ee864c5c4e6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f11cbcb19122281","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-59hfl4mw/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-BRANCH-B-E006.md","content":"# Elapsed-time progress display for running evaluation jobs\n\n## Description\n\nBranch B of the progress-display work, selected if the benchmark data-availability investigation finds that `status.benchmarks[]` is only populated in the EvalHub detail endpoint upon job completion. In this outcome there is no mid-run data worth polling the detail endpoint for, so no detail-polling layer is built: running jobs display elapsed time as the primary progress indicator, computed client-side from the job's `resource.created_at` (available on the list endpoint), alongside the top-level state from the existing list polling. This matches the strategy's stated fallback for this outcome: \"the UI can only show elapsed time + overall state\".\n\n## Scope\n\n- Elapsed-time display for non-terminal (running/pending) jobs on the Evaluations landing page, computed client-side as the difference between the current time and the job's `resource.created_at` from the list endpoint response.\n- Presentation per the UX specification's progress indicator pattern (elapsed time as the primary indicator), including for single-benchmark jobs where benchmark completion would show only 0% or 100%.\n- Client-side periodic refresh of the elapsed display without manual page refresh; top-level state continues to come from the existing 30-second list-endpoint polling.\n- No mid-run detail-endpoint polling in this branch; the existing list polling and table rendering continue to function unchanged.\n- Terminal-state jobs stop showing a running elapsed timer and may show final duration where per-benchmark timestamps are available post-completion.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a job that has been running for 4 minutes, the row displays elapsed time (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\"), measured by the difference between the current time and the job's `resource.created_at`, updating without manual browser refresh.\n- The elapsed-time presentation follows the UX specification's progress indicator pattern (elapsed time as the primary indicator).\n- No requests are made to the detail endpoint for mid-run progress in this branch; top-level state continues to be provided by the existing list-endpoint polling.\n- The existing list-endpoint polling and table rendering continue to function unchanged.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-5 (P1, elapsed time display for running jobs): primary delivery in this branch (computed from `resource.created_at`).\n- HLR-4 (P1, benchmark-level progress) and HLR-6 (P1, detail-polling pause on backgrounded tabs) are not deliverable in this branch — the existing API provides no mid-run benchmark data — and require a strategy-level descope decision, as flagged in the decomposition health warnings.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":72315,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9970d42ea05d3b5f","agent_id":"a9be68a0f929ee067","session_id":"f9ae5287-b92a-4025-94c1-a1778be86910","uuid":"920fec50-086c-4b70-82c5-7d55b5b26bea","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:28:22.813Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
