{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9269fb7024254765","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate mid-run availability of benchmark status in the EvalHub job detail\n4\t  API\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n6\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n7\tteam: TrustyAI / EvalHub\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 1\n13\t  source_accessibility: 1\n14\t  local_runnability: 0\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n16\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Validate mid-run availability of benchmark status in the EvalHub job detail API\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's flagged open question: does the EvalHub Server detail endpoint (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) populate `status.benchmarks[]` entries — per-benchmark status with `started_at`/`completed_at` — while an evaluation job is still running, or only after the job completes? The answer determines which progress-display implementation is built: a detail-polling layer with benchmark-level progress (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") and elapsed time derived from per-benchmark `started_at`, or an elapsed-time-only display computed from `resource.created_at` on the list endpoint. The strategy's assumption that the array is populated mid-run is explicitly marked \"needs validation\", and the Staff Engineer Input's field-availability table documents only that the field exists in the response schema, not when it is populated during execution.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Determine, from the EvalHub Server source code (the job status write paths) and, where feasible, observed API responses, when `status.benchmarks[]` entries are created and updated over a job's lifecycle.\n35\t- Document which fields are present per benchmark entry mid-run (status values, `started_at`, `completed_at`) and whether entries appear at benchmark start, update incrementally, or appear only at completion.\n36\t- Capture sample detail-endpoint responses for a job in a non-terminal (running) state where a live environment is available.\n37\t- Record the outcome so the branch selection for the progress-display work is unambiguous: mid-run population (detail polling with benchmark progress) or completion-only population (elapsed-time-only display), including any partial-population behavior discovered.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- A findings report states whether `status.benchmarks[]` is populated while a job is in a running state or only upon completion, with cited evidence (EvalHub Server source references and/or captured detail-endpoint responses from a running job).\n42\t- Where mid-run population occurs, the report documents which per-benchmark fields are present mid-run and when entries appear or update relative to benchmark start/completion.\n43\t- The report identifies any partial-population behavior (e.g., entries appearing at benchmark start but status updating only at completion) and states which progress-display presentation that behavior supports.\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability\n46\t\n47\t- HLR-4 (P1, benchmark-level progress display): this investigation determines whether HLR-4 is deliverable against the existing API.\n48\t- HLR-5 (P1, elapsed time display): determines the timestamp source (per-benchmark `started_at` vs `resource.created_at`) for the elapsed-time computation.\n49\t- HLR-1 (P0, auto-refresh/detail polling portion): determines whether the detail-polling layer has mid-run data to fetch.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9ca683fd5a24274","agent_id":"a19e66e98275a5ef3","session_id":"f9ae5287-b92a-4025-94c1-a1778be86910","uuid":"7a6ec9f5-3af7-4eab-8339-184895746ae2","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:31:37.930Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9269fb7024254765","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
