{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88a5016d4b64e154","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E002\n3\ttitle: Catalogue EvalHub failure message codes for pre-start vs runtime failures\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: TrustyAI / EvalHub\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Catalogue EvalHub failure message codes for pre-start vs runtime failures\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's flagged open question: what values does `status.message.message_code` take in the EvalHub job list/detail responses, and do those values reliably distinguish pre-start failures (admission errors, scheduling failures, resource constraints) from runtime failures? The answer determines whether the UI can render \"Failed (not started)\" as a visually distinct state from runtime \"Failed\", or must fall back to a single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail — a fallback the strategy already defines in its risk table.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Enumerate the values `status.message.message_code` can take, from the EvalHub Server source code (the error paths that construct status messages) and the published API reference.\n34\t- Classify each value as indicating a pre-start failure (admission error, scheduling failure, resource quota/constraint), a runtime failure, or unclassifiable from the code alone.\n35\t- Where a live environment is available, capture observed `message_code` values from jobs that failed before start and jobs that failed during execution.\n36\t- Produce a recommendation stating whether the pre-start vs runtime distinction is reliably implementable in the UI from `message_code` alone, enabling the gated failure-distinction work to proceed or be removed in favor of the defined fallback.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A catalogue lists the `status.message.message_code` values attainable in list and detail endpoint responses, each with its meaning and a source citation (EvalHub Server source and/or API reference).\n41\t- Every catalogued value is classified as pre-start failure, runtime failure, or unclassifiable.\n42\t- A recommendation states whether the pre-start vs runtime failure distinction is implementable from `message_code` alone, and — if not — explicitly confirms the fallback of a single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- HLR-7 (P2, pre-start vs runtime failure distinction): this investigation determines whether HLR-7 is implementable as specified or falls back to the single-state rendering.\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9ca683fd5a24274","agent_id":"a19e66e98275a5ef3","session_id":"f9ae5287-b92a-4025-94c1-a1778be86910","uuid":"c35c8c04-e005-4f5e-b1e6-695c546f8a68","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:31:38.614Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-88a5016d4b64e154","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
