{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-965f184532236111","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E003\n3\ttitle: Progress indicator and job state UX specification for the EvalHub Evaluations\n4\t  page\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n6\tcomponent: UXD\n7\tteam: UX/Design\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: -1\n19\t  repo_access: 0\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Progress indicator and job state UX specification for the EvalHub Evaluations page\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic produces the \"progress indicator UX specification\" design document that the strategy lists as to-be-created, authored by UX/Design. It defines the visual and interaction patterns the EvalHub Evaluations landing page implementations build against: state icon/color/label treatments for queued/pending, running, failed, and completed jobs, the progress indicator pattern (elapsed time primary, benchmark completion count supplementary), the \"Failed (not started)\" variant treatment, and the non-blocking warning pattern for temporarily unavailable status updates — all aligned to PatternFly.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- State visual specifications: distinct PatternFly Label/Icon/color treatments for queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states derived from the list endpoint's `status.state`, including a \"Failed (not started)\" variant distinct from runtime \"Failed\".\n39\t- Progress indicator pattern for running jobs: elapsed time as the primary indicator (mitigating the single-benchmark-job risk, where benchmark completion shows only 0% or 100%), with benchmark completion count (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") as supplementary when available. The pattern must cover both the benchmark-progress presentation and the elapsed-time-only presentation.\n40\t- Non-blocking inline warning pattern for transient polling errors: PatternFly Alert variant \"warning\", rendered while stale (last successful) data continues to display.\n41\t- PatternFly alignment review across the above, using the dashboard design system conventions.\n42\t- The specification is written to hold under either outcome of the benchmark data-availability validation (elapsed-time-primary is the presentation in both cases), so it does not wait on that investigation.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- The specification defines icon, color, and label treatments for queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states, each visually distinct per the PatternFly status pattern.\n47\t- The specification defines the \"Failed (not started)\" treatment as distinguishable from the runtime \"Failed\" treatment.\n48\t- The specification defines the progress indicator pattern with elapsed time as the primary indicator and benchmark completion count as supplementary.\n49\t- The specification defines the non-blocking inline warning pattern for temporarily unavailable status updates using PatternFly Alert variant \"warning\".\n50\t- The specification is completed and accepted by the ODH Dashboard implementing team as the build-against reference for the evaluations page UI work.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- No HLR is delivered solely by this epic; it is the design prerequisite for HLR-2 (P0, state visual distinction), HLR-4 and HLR-5 (P1, benchmark progress and elapsed time display), and HLR-7 (P2, failure distinction). Functional delivery of those HLRs occurs in the implementation epics that consume this specification.\n55\t"}]},