{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-831c10f1fdd44de2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E004\n3\ttitle: State visual differentiation for the EvalHub evaluations job list\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E003\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: -1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# State visual differentiation for the EvalHub evaluations job list\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic delivers visually distinct state treatments on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page job table, derived from the list endpoint's `status.state` and `status.message` fields: queued/pending, running, failed, and completed, each with a distinct PatternFly status icon, color, and label per the UX specification. It also delivers the fallback failure rendering — a single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail — which stands on its own if the finer pre-start/runtime failure distinction proves unimplementable.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Render state labels, icons, and color treatments for queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states from the list endpoint's `status.state` field, per the UX specification's state treatments.\n39\t- Display error context from `status.message` on failed job rows.\n40\t- Render the baseline single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail where failure classification is not available (the defined fallback).\n41\t- Preserve the existing list-endpoint polling (30s via `useFetchState`) and table rendering behavior unchanged — the state differentiation is additive (backwards-compatibility NFR).\n42\t- No detail-endpoint polling is introduced in this epic; this scope uses only list-endpoint fields, whose availability is confirmed.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- Job rows display a distinct label, icon, and color for each of queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states derived from `status.state`, visually distinguishable from each other per the UX specification.\n47\t- A job transitioning from running to complete is reflected in the job list within the existing list-endpoint polling interval (30 seconds) without manual browser refresh, measured by the row's state label updating automatically.\n48\t- Failed job rows display error context from `status.message`.\n49\t- Where failure classification is unavailable, the row renders the single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail.\n50\t- The existing list-endpoint polling and table rendering continue to function unchanged.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- HLR-1 (P0, auto-refresh showing state transitions without manual refresh): delivers the top-level state-transition visibility driven by the existing list-endpoint polling. (The detail-polling portion of HLR-1 is delivered by the branch-conditional progress work.)\n55\t- HLR-2 (P0, visual distinction between queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states): primary delivery.\n56\t- HLR-7 (P2, pre-start vs runtime failure distinction): delivers the fallback baseline rendering only; the distinction itself is delivered by the gated failure-distinction work.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9ca683fd5a24274","agent_id":"a19e66e98275a5ef3","session_id":"f9ae5287-b92a-4025-94c1-a1778be86910","uuid":"61765b52-89af-4ac2-af6d-73481226a881","timestamp":"2026-1