{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91cb75bb09a079c5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E005\n3\ttitle: Pre-start vs runtime failure distinction in the evaluations job list\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E002\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E004\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E002\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: 'If message_code values do not reliably distinguish pre-start\n16\t    from runtime failures, remove this epic and keep the fallback already delivered\n17\t    by the state differentiation work: a single ''Failed'' state with status.message\n18\t    text as supplementary detail.'\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 5\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Pre-start vs runtime failure distinction in the evaluations job list\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tThis epic delivers the finer failure-state distinction on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page: rendering \"Failed (not started)\" — with a label, icon, and color distinct from runtime \"Failed\" — for jobs whose `status.message.message_code` indicates a pre-start failure (admission error, scheduling failure, resource constraint), per the validated message-code catalogue and the UX specification's failure-variant treatment. If the catalogue finds the values do not reliably distinguish failure types, this epic is removed and the fallback (single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text) delivered by the state differentiation work stands.\n41\t\n42\t## Description of Dependencies\n43\t\n44\tThis epic is gated on the validated `message_code` semantics catalogue and builds on the state rendering surface delivered by the state differentiation work and its UX specification; those must resolve first.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Apply the validated `status.message.message_code` classification to failed job rows: render \"Failed (not started)\" where the code indicates a pre-start failure (admission error, scheduling failure, resource constraint), and runtime \"Failed\" otherwise.\n49\t- Render the distinct label, icon, and color for the \"Failed (not started)\" variant per the UX specification's failure treatments.\n50\t- Where `message_code` is ambiguous or absent, fall back to the single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail.\n51\t- No new API fields, enum values, or server-side changes — the distinction works within the existing list-endpoint data (strategy constraint).\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Given a job that failed before execution started, with `status.message.message_code` classified as a pre-start failure per the validated catalogue, the job row displays a \"Failed (not started)\" treatment with label, icon, and color distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state.\n56\t- Given a job that ran and then failed, the job row displays the runtime \"Failed\" treatment.\n57\t- Where `message_code` is ambiguous or absent, the job row falls back to the single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- HLR-7 (P2, pre-start vs runtime failure distinction using `status.message.message_code` where available): primary delivery.\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9ca683fd5a24274","agent_id":"a19e66e98275a5ef3","session_id":"f9ae5287-b92a-4025-94c1-a1778be86910","uuid":"a6a2980d-e1d0-4109-a38c-dd41b4b998d0","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:31:47.628Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-91cb75bb09a079c5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
