{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f7465e7d2d678eb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-BRANCH-A-E006\n3\ttitle: Detail-polling layer with benchmark progress and elapsed time for in-progress\n4\t  evaluation jobs\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n6\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n7\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tbranch: A\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E003\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: rewrite\n17\t  fallback_approach: 'If status.benchmarks[] is only populated upon job completion,\n18\t    this epic is replaced by the elapsed-time-only display (branch B): no mid-run\n19\t    detail polling, elapsed time computed from resource.created_at on the list endpoint.'\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: 1\n26\t  external_dependency: 1\n27\t  human_process_gates: -1\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 7\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Detail-polling layer with benchmark progress and elapsed time for in-progress evaluation jobs\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tBranch A of the progress-display work, selected if the benchmark data-availability investigation confirms that `status.benchmarks[]` is populated in the EvalHub detail endpoint (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) while a job is running. This epic delivers the new detail-polling layer for the Evaluations landing page: a hook that identifies non-terminal jobs on the currently displayed table page and fetches their detail endpoints on a 10-second cycle with a maximum of 5 concurrent requests in round-robin, adopting the React Query retry-with-backoff pattern established by the autorag package. It renders benchmark-level progress (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\"), elapsed time from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps, and a non-blocking inline warning during transient errors. Polling pauses when the browser tab is backgrounded.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Detail-polling hook targeting only non-terminal jobs on the currently displayed table page (client-side pagination: default 20 rows, options 5/10/20); changing the table page immediately retargets which jobs are polled.\n45\t- Concurrency control: maximum 5 concurrent detail requests per user session, dispatched in round-robin (as one request completes, the next pending job is fetched); a 10-second timer starts after all detail fetches for the current page complete, before the next cycle.\n46\t- Retry-on-error per the autorag `usePipelineRunQuery` pattern: `placeholderData` preserving the last successful response, exponential backoff with jitter up to the configured maximum retries, 4xx errors treated as non-retryable, 5xx/network errors retried; a single failed request does not stop the round-robin (partial progress data is acceptable).\n47\t- Non-blocking inline warning (PatternFly Alert variant \"warning\") while status updates are temporarily unavailable, with the last successfully fetched data still displayed.\n48\t- Benchmark-level progress display: \"Benchmarks: X/N complete\" where X is the count of `status.benchmarks[]` entries with status \"completed\", presented as supplementary to the elapsed-time primary indicator per the UX specification.\n49\t- Elapsed time display: client-side difference between current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` across benchmarks (falling back to `resource.created_at` if no benchmark has started).\n50\t- Page Visibility API integration: polling pauses when the tab is backgrounded and resumes with an immediate single polling cycle on focus; polling stops for terminal-state jobs.\n51\t- Until the first detail fetch returns for a job, the row shows only the top-level state from the list endpoint (graceful degradation if the detail endpoint is unavailable).\n52\t- Verification (passive component validation): confirm the odh-dashboard BFF proxy passes through all detail response fields from the eval-hub plugin backend — including `status.benchmarks[]` — without filtering; no BFF code change is expected.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Given a running job with 3 of 5 benchmarks completed and a completed detail-polling cycle for that job, the row displays benchmark-level progress (\"Benchmarks: 3/5 complete\"), measured by the count matching the number of `status.benchmarks[]` entries with status \"completed\" in the detail response.\n57\t- Given a job running for 4 minutes with a completed detail fetch, elapsed time is displayed (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\"), measured by the difference between current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` in the detail response.\n58\t- At most 5 detail requests are in flight concurrently per user session, targeted only at non-terminal jobs on the currently displayed table page; changing the table page immediately updates which jobs are polled.\n59\t- Given a 5xx or network error on a detail fetch, the last successfully fetched progress remains displayed, a non-blocking inline warning (PatternFly Alert variant \"warning\") is visible, the round-robin continues with the next in-progress job, and the failed request retries with exponential backoff up to the configured maximum; 4xx errors are not retried.\n60\t- While the browser tab is backgrounded, no requests are made to the detail endpoint (verified via browser dev tools Network tab); on tab focus, a single polling cycle runs immediately.\n61\t- Polling stops for jobs that reach a terminal state.\n62\t- The React Query retry pattern is validated in the eval-hub Module Federation context by simulating 5xx errors from the BFF on individual detail endpoints (risk-mitigation validation; failure means fix-and-retry within this epic).\n63\t- The BFF proxy is verified to pass through all detail response fields, including `status.benchmarks[]`, without filtering.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-1 (P0, auto-refresh mechanism — detail endpoint polling portion): primary delivery of the detail-polling layer.\n68\t- HLR-3 (P0, non-blocking error handling during detail polling): retry with exponential backoff, stale data preserved, inline warning.\n69\t- HLR-4 (P1, benchmark-level progress display with max-5 round-robin fetch): primary delivery.\n70\t- HLR-5 (P1, elapsed time display from per-benchmark `started_at`): primary delivery.\n71\t- HLR-6 (P1, polling pauses on backgrounded tab and resumes on focus): primary delivery.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9ca683fd5a24274","agent_id":"a19e66e98275a5ef3","session_id":"f9ae5287-b92a-4025-94c1-a1778be86910","uuid":"725bf357-f2f7-42b4-a359-4db4bbc9bbff","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:31:48.460Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f7465e7d2d678eb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
