{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-861bed7c74714fa5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-BRANCH-B-E006\n3\ttitle: Elapsed-time progress display for running evaluation jobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E003\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If status.benchmarks[] is populated mid-run, this epic is replaced\n17\t    by the full detail-polling implementation with benchmark-level progress (branch\n18\t    A).\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 7\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Elapsed-time progress display for running evaluation jobs\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tBranch B of the progress-display work, selected if the benchmark data-availability investigation finds that `status.benchmarks[]` is only populated in the EvalHub detail endpoint upon job completion. In this outcome there is no mid-run data worth polling the detail endpoint for, so no detail-polling layer is built: running jobs display elapsed time as the primary progress indicator, computed client-side from the job's `resource.created_at` (available on the list endpoint), alongside the top-level state from the existing list polling. This matches the strategy's stated fallback for this outcome: \"the UI can only show elapsed time + overall state\".\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Elapsed-time display for non-terminal (running/pending) jobs on the Evaluations landing page, computed client-side as the difference between the current time and the job's `resource.created_at` from the list endpoint response.\n44\t- Presentation per the UX specification's progress indicator pattern (elapsed time as the primary indicator), including for single-benchmark jobs where benchmark completion would show only 0% or 100%.\n45\t- Client-side periodic refresh of the elapsed display without manual page refresh; top-level state continues to come from the existing 30-second list-endpoint polling.\n46\t- No mid-run detail-endpoint polling in this branch; the existing list polling and table rendering continue to function unchanged.\n47\t- Terminal-state jobs stop showing a running elapsed timer and may show final duration where per-benchmark timestamps are available post-completion.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given a job that has been running for 4 minutes, the row displays elapsed time (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\"), measured by the difference between the current time and the job's `resource.created_at`, updating without manual browser refresh.\n52\t- The elapsed-time presentation follows the UX specification's progress indicator pattern (elapsed time as the primary indicator).\n53\t- No requests are made to the detail endpoint for mid-run progress in this branch; top-level state continues to be provided by the existing list-endpoint polling.\n54\t- The existing list-endpoint polling and table rendering continue to function unchanged.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR-5 (P1, elapsed time display for running jobs): primary delivery in this branch (computed from `resource.created_at`).\n59\t- HLR-4 (P1, benchmark-level progress) and HLR-6 (P1, detail-polling pause on backgrounded tabs) are not deliverable in this branch — the existing API provides no mid-run benchmark data — and require a strategy-level descope decision, as flagged in the decomposition health warnings.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9ca683fd5a24274","agent_id":"a19e66e98275a5ef3","session_id":"f9ae5287-b92a-4025-94c1-a1778be86910","uuid":"b3a99105-d953-4f43-af89-b93f445536b1","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:31:52.210Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-861bed7c74714fa5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
